###############################################################################
# QuantPulse environment template
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development:   cp .env.example .env.local
# .env.local is gitignored. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# The app runs with NONE of these set. They only become necessary once it is
# deployed behind a real domain.
#
# On Vercel, add these under Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables and
# pick the right scope (Production / Preview / Development).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD time and are
# publicly readable. Anything secret must NOT carry that prefix.
###############################################################################

# --- Application -------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical origin, no trailing slash. This is also the CORS allow-list entry
# for /api/history: if it is wrong, cross-origin browser calls are rejected.
# (Same-origin calls — what the app itself makes — work regardless.)
#
# Local:      http://localhost:3000
# Production: https://quantpulse.io
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional extra browser origins allowed to call the API, comma separated.
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://www.quantpulse.io,https://staging.quantpulse.io


# --- Market data -------------------------------------------------------------
# Prices come from Yahoo Finance via the `yahoo-finance2` package, which needs
# no API key or account. There is deliberately nothing to configure here.
#
# If you later swap in a keyed provider (Alpha Vantage, Financial Modeling Prep,
# Polygon), add its key here as a SERVER-side variable — never NEXT_PUBLIC_ —
# and read it in src/lib/market.ts, which is already server-only.
# MARKET_DATA_API_KEY=


# --- News sentiment (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# Enables the sixth factor, "News sentiment", from Alpha Vantage's
# NEWS_SENTIMENT endpoint. Without this key the factor is hidden — the other
# five are unaffected.
#
# Free key: https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key
#
# Caveat worth knowing before you rely on it: the free tier is heavily rate
# limited and one response covers a bounded window of articles, so it usually
# yields weeks of history rather than years. The factor reports its own
# coverage and suppresses its statistics when the sample is too short to mean
# anything. Trusting it needs a premium key.
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=
